- Affected when the player is moving, traveling, changing location, navigating terrain,
  climbing, swimming, jumping, falling, flying, mounting, dismounting, or being
  displaced (pushed, knocked back, carried).
- Short movements within a scene still count if mechanically relevant: crossing a room,
  approaching NPCs or objects, climbing a wall, jumping a gap, swimming across a channel.
- Affected when the action is about proximity to world elements: approaching or moving
  toward NPCs, creatures, objects, or landmarks. "I approach the goblins", "I move
  toward the lake", "I get closer to the altar" all affect traversal.
- Climbing, swimming, and jumping are traversal actions even if the player doesn't
  phrase them as movement. "I climb the wall", "I swim across", "I leap the gap"
  are all traversal because they change where the player can go.
- Falling is traversal because it changes position and the physical state of movement.
- Mounting or dismounting a creature is traversal when it changes how the player is moving.
- destination: the name of a STORY LOCATION the player is actively traveling toward,
  only when they have not yet arrived. Set to null for short movements within
  the current location or when targeting an entity rather than a named location.
- Traversal does NOT own stealth. If the player is sneaking, hiding, shadowing,
  moving quietly, or trying not to be noticed while moving, leave stealth
  adjudication to exploration.
- When combat is active and the player attempts to flee, escape, or disengage from
  the fight: affected true, transition null. Do NOT set transition "combat_ended" — CombatGM
  adjudicates success or failure and ends combat only on a successful escape.
